##
## Deprecated CA Root Certificates
## Deprecated CA Root Certificates that get appended to 'cacrt_all.pem'

## These certificates have been removed from the newer Mozilla CA certificate store.
## Refer to https://wiki.mozilla.org/CA/Removed_Certificates for more information.

## These certificates might be removed from ESP-IDF during every major release.

## The current deprecated certificate bundle is up-to-date with the Mozilla cert bundle (cacrt_all.pem) dated Thu Nov  5 04:12:01 2026 GMT

## Not included on purpose, although unexpired:
##   emSign ECC Root CA - G3: root of the compromised eMudhra G3 intermediates
##     (Mozilla bug 2083449).
##   Comodo AAA Services root: Sectigo cross-signed the same intermediates
##     (Mozilla bug 2083449).
##   E-Tugra Global Root CA RSA v3 and ECC v3: removed by Mozilla after
##     E-Tugra's security breach (Mozilla bug 1842928).
##   Entrust Root Certification Authority, - G2, - EC1 and - G4,
##     Entrust.net Premium 2048 Secure Server CA, and AffirmTrust Commercial,
##     Networking, Premium and Premium ECC: Mozilla distrusted Entrust for TLS
##     after compliance failures (Mozilla bug 1922387).
##   Autoridad de Certificacion Firmaprofesional CIF A62634068 (2009): its
##     2014 reissue in cacrt_all.pem has the same name.
## Do not re-add them when syncing with ESP-IDF. A chain that ends in a
## cross-sign issued by one of these still verifies when the cross-signed CA is
## itself a bundle root (e.g. USERTrust ECC/RSA cross-signed by AAA).


